# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/upload-1 window (docs/tp4-upload1.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-upload-1-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed head of tp4/upload-1 (the ship-5 stack plus the host tier's upload levers, qwen_tier_upload;
# substitute it in every template with one command: sed -i 's/tp4-upload-1-1/<tag>/' *.env). THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that exists. The levers live in files the image carries
# (qwen_tier_upload.py, qwen_prefix_registry.py, qwen_prefix_scheduler_patch.py): an image built before them ignores the three names and the arm reads NOT_EXERCISED (no "host tier upload on" line).
# The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent (production is down by the owner's choice while it runs).
# U5 (TIMED, the ABAB's B repeat, the LEVERS): the tier-timed cycle at ~64k, ~128k and ~254k (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-upload-timed, scenario tier_upload_timed: no row digests, no extent audit, the tier's own audits off, the digest
# check sampled) on the ship-5 candidate c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5, which is the PRODUCTION profile (the sliced restore is on in it). THE LEVERS: QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_IO_THREADS=4 and QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_VERIFY_THREADS=4 added by the gate. THE ABAB: U2 control, U3 upload, U4 control repeat, U5 upload repeat, every boot a
# fresh reset, the ARC runner sets at ZERO for the job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO): no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. The pair differs by exactly the env the gate derives (no profile twin).
# READ each: the plan verdict PASS (every cold twin IDENTICAL to its returning hit), the "host tier restore" line of each returning turn (blocks, GB, ms; with the sliced restore on, slices= and the sum of
# the slices' work), c2_smoke_check clean; then the four together: python3 scripts/ci/upload_restore_compare.py <U2 results> <U3 results> <U4 results> <U5 results> (A control, B upload, C control repeat,
# D upload repeat): GO needs, in both pairs, every returning answer IDENTICAL to the control's, the restore's ms at 128k and 254k lower by at least 25% and the returning hit's TTFT at no size higher than the
# control's by more than the larger of 5% and the control-to-control floor. ESTIMATE (the CPU bench with the device simulated at Q1's rates, docs/tp4-upload1.md; nothing here has run on a card): the 254k
# restore falls from about 0.96 s (T3: 8.56 GB at 8.9 GB/s) toward the device-write time, about 0.4 to 0.5 s; the returning hit's first token (6.5 s whole in T3, reported as about 5.4 s on this profile) falls by the same
# fraction of a second and no more (the tail prefill and the engine build, 4.2 to 4.8 s, are not an upload). Unqualified: a measurement, never evidence. Estimate: 45 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-upload-1-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-upload-timed
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
